WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.865
Salary Negotiation.

2
00:00:02.145 --> 00:00:06.049
Day 89 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Career phase.

3
00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:08.823
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.103 --> 00:00:14.799
Companies expect you to negotiate, and a calm, data-backed ask is professional, not rude.

5
00:00:15.079 --> 00:00:21.180
A few uncomfortable minutes can change your earnings for years, because every future raise builds on this number.

6
00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:23.383
Part 1.

7
00:00:23.663 --> 00:00:25.114
The negotiation flow.

8
00:00:26.364 --> 00:00:27.281
Step 1:

9
00:00:27.561 --> 00:00:31.252
Research: know your market value (range, not a single number).

10
00:00:31.532 --> 00:00:32.449
Step 2:

11
00:00:32.729 --> 00:00:35.631
Prepare: your wins, your target, your walk-away number.

12
00:00:35.911 --> 00:00:36.828
Step 3:

13
00:00:37.108 --> 00:00:39.967
Delay the number: let them anchor first when possible.

14
00:00:40.247 --> 00:00:41.207
Step 4:

15
00:00:41.487 --> 00:00:44.921
Respond: thank, show enthusiasm, then counter with data.

16
00:00:45.201 --> 00:00:46.161
Step 5:

17
00:00:46.441 --> 00:00:49.855
Trade: negotiate the whole package, not only base pay.

18
00:00:50.135 --> 00:00:51.073
Step 6:

19
00:00:51.353 --> 00:00:53.465
Close: confirm everything in writing.

20
00:00:54.815 --> 00:00:55.690
Part 2.

21
00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:56.887
Step 1:

22
00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:58.277
Know your numbers.

23
00:00:59.527 --> 00:01:00.892
Here is a quick table:

24
00:01:01.172 --> 00:01:03.348
Number, and What it means, and Example.

25
00:01:03.628 --> 00:01:04.631
Market range.

26
00:01:04.911 --> 00:01:05.807
What it means:

27
00:01:06.087 --> 00:01:09.180
What similar roles pay (level, city, company type).

28
00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:10.335
Example:

29
00:01:10.615 --> 00:01:13.025
45 rupees, 60 LPA.

30
00:01:13.305 --> 00:01:14.095
Target.

31
00:01:14.375 --> 00:01:15.271
What it means:

32
00:01:15.551 --> 00:01:18.815
What you'll ask for: upper part of the range, backed by data.

33
00:01:19.095 --> 00:01:19.969
Example:

34
00:01:20.249 --> 00:01:22.319
58 lakh per annum rupees.

35
00:01:22.599 --> 00:01:23.473
Walk-away.

36
00:01:23.753 --> 00:01:24.649
What it means:

37
00:01:24.929 --> 00:01:26.487
Below this, you decline.

38
00:01:26.767 --> 00:01:28.580
Decide before the conversation.

39
00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:29.735
Example:

40
00:01:30.015 --> 00:01:31.700
50 lakh per annum rupees.

41
00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:40.453
Sources: salary sites (Glassdoor, AmbitionBox, Levels.fyi), recruiters, trusted peers, industry reports.

42
00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:45.597
Compare the same level and city, and compare total compensation, not just base.

43
00:01:46.947 --> 00:01:47.843
Part 3.

44
00:01:48.123 --> 00:01:49.040
Step 2:

45
00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.643
Build your value case.

46
00:01:51.893 --> 00:01:54.431
Write down 3 to 5 achievements with numbers:

47
00:01:54.711 --> 00:02:02.455
Led the checkout re-architecture, which cut failures 60% and protected ~2 crore rupees in sale-day revenue.

48
00:02:02.735 --> 00:02:06.341
Reduced cloud costs by 35 lakh rupees per year.

49
00:02:06.621 --> 00:02:09.053
Mentored 4 engineers; 2 were promoted.

50
00:02:09.333 --> 00:02:12.149
Cut deploy time from 2 hours to 18 minutes.

51
00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:14.416
Part 4.

52
00:02:14.696 --> 00:02:16.275
Scripts: new job offer.

53
00:02:17.525 --> 00:02:21.279
\What are your salary expectations?\ (early).

54
00:02:21.559 --> 00:02:22.498
You could say:

55
00:02:22.778 --> 00:02:26.213
I'd like to understand the role and responsibilities better first.

56
00:02:26.493 --> 00:02:29.159
Could you share the budgeted range for this position?

57
00:02:30.509 --> 00:02:31.704
If they insist:

58
00:02:33.054 --> 00:02:33.993
You could say:

59
00:02:34.273 --> 00:02:46.582
Based on my research for senior backend roles in Bangalore with my experience, I'm looking in the range of 55 rupeesto 62 lakh total compensation, depending on the overall package.

60
00:02:47.932 --> 00:02:51.239
Give a range whose bottom is still a number you'd be happy with.

61
00:02:52.589 --> 00:02:55.042
\What's your current salary?\.

62
00:02:55.322 --> 00:02:56.261
You could say:

63
00:02:56.541 --> 00:02:59.079
I'd prefer to focus on the value of this role.

64
00:02:59.359 --> 00:03:04.949
My expectation is based on the market and what I bring, which is around 58 lakh rupees.

65
00:03:06.299 --> 00:03:09.371
(In some places, employers may ask for payslips.

66
00:03:09.651 --> 00:03:11.016
Be honest if you share.

67
00:03:11.296 --> 00:03:12.405
Never inflate.).

68
00:03:13.755 --> 00:03:15.227
Responding to the offer.

69
00:03:15.507 --> 00:03:16.446
You could say:

70
00:03:16.726 --> 00:03:19.713
Thank you, I'm really excited about this role and the team.

71
00:03:19.993 --> 00:03:21.273
I've reviewed the offer.

72
00:03:21.553 --> 00:03:30.086
Given my experience leading high-scale payment systems and the market range for this level, I was expecting closer to 58 lakh rupees.

73
00:03:30.366 --> 00:03:32.222
Is there flexibility on the base?

74
00:03:33.572 --> 00:03:35.684
Then stop talking and let them respond.

75
00:03:35.964 --> 00:03:37.756
The silence works in your favour.

76
00:03:39.106 --> 00:03:41.943
They say \This is our best offer\.

77
00:03:42.223 --> 00:03:43.162
You could say:

78
00:03:43.442 --> 00:03:45.426
I understand the base may be fixed.

79
00:03:45.706 --> 00:03:53.471
Could we look at other parts of the package: a joining bonus, extra ESOPs, or a salary review after 6 months instead of 12?

80
00:03:54.821 --> 00:03:55.931
Competing offer.

81
00:03:56.211 --> 00:03:57.149
You could say:

82
00:03:57.429 --> 00:03:58.923
I want to be transparent:

83
00:03:59.203 --> 00:04:01.656
I have another offer at 60 lakh rupees.

84
00:04:01.936 --> 00:04:05.477
This role is my first choice because of the product and the team.

85
00:04:05.757 --> 00:04:08.957
If you can get closer to that, I'm ready to accept this week.

86
00:04:10.307 --> 00:04:11.886
Only say this if it's true.

87
00:04:12.166 --> 00:04:13.894
Bluffing can backfire badly.

88
00:04:15.244 --> 00:04:16.183
Accepting.

89
00:04:16.463 --> 00:04:17.401
You could say:

90
00:04:17.681 --> 00:04:19.281
Thank you, that works for me.

91
00:04:19.561 --> 00:04:20.863
I'm happy to accept.

92
00:04:21.143 --> 00:04:26.967
Could you send the updated offer letter with the base, joining bonus and ESOP details so I can sign it?

93
00:04:28.317 --> 00:04:29.277
Part 5.

94
00:04:29.557 --> 00:04:31.583
Scripts: raise at your current company.

95
00:04:32.833 --> 00:04:34.092
Asking for the meeting.

96
00:04:34.372 --> 00:04:35.311
You could say:

97
00:04:35.591 --> 00:04:39.900
Could we set up 30 minutes next week to discuss my compensation and growth?

98
00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:43.209
I'd like to prepare properly, so I wanted to give you notice.

99
00:04:44.559 --> 00:04:45.669
Making the case.

100
00:04:45.949 --> 00:04:46.887
You could say:

101
00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:55.039
Over the last year I've led the checkout migration, reduced cloud costs by 35 lakh rupees, and mentored four engineers.

102
00:04:55.319 --> 00:04:59.373
My responsibilities have grown to include architecture for two teams.

103
00:04:59.653 --> 00:05:06.394
Based on that and market data for this level, I'd like to discuss an adjustment to around 58 lakh rupees.

104
00:05:06.674 --> 00:05:08.423
What would it take to make that happen?

105
00:05:09.773 --> 00:05:12.355
If the answer is \not now\.

106
00:05:12.635 --> 00:05:13.573
You could say:

107
00:05:13.853 --> 00:05:15.624
I understand the budget timing.

108
00:05:15.904 --> 00:05:20.064
Could we agree on specific goals and a date to revisit, say in 3 months?

109
00:05:20.344 --> 00:05:23.203
I'd also appreciate it in writing so we're both clear.

110
00:05:24.553 --> 00:05:25.491
Part 6.

111
00:05:25.771 --> 00:05:27.371
Negotiate the whole package.

112
00:05:28.621 --> 00:05:29.987
Here is a quick table:

113
00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:31.888
Component, and What to ask.

114
00:05:32.168 --> 00:05:33.213
Base salary:

115
00:05:33.493 --> 00:05:36.267
The main number; every future hike builds on it.

116
00:05:36.547 --> 00:05:38.253
Joining or sign-on bonus:

117
00:05:38.533 --> 00:05:41.115
Covers bonus or ESOPs you lose by leaving.

118
00:05:41.395 --> 00:05:43.229
Variable or performance bonus:

119
00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:47.456
Target %, how it's measured, how often it's paid out in practice.

120
00:05:47.736 --> 00:05:49.059
ESOPs or RSUs:

121
00:05:49.339 --> 00:05:52.389
Number, vesting schedule, cliff, current valuation.

122
00:05:52.669 --> 00:05:53.843
Title or level:

123
00:05:54.123 --> 00:05:56.277
Affects future pay and your next job.

124
00:05:56.557 --> 00:05:57.965
Notice-period buyout:

125
00:05:58.245 --> 00:05:59.909
If your current notice is long.

126
00:06:00.189 --> 00:06:01.469
Remote or hybrid:

127
00:06:01.749 --> 00:06:04.032
Days in office, home-office allowance.

128
00:06:04.312 --> 00:06:05.443
Learning budget:

129
00:06:05.723 --> 00:06:07.557
Certifications, conferences.

130
00:06:08.907 --> 00:06:10.017
Review timeline:

131
00:06:10.297 --> 00:06:11.811
Early review at 6 months.

132
00:06:12.091 --> 00:06:13.094
Relocation:

133
00:06:13.374 --> 00:06:15.038
Travel, temporary housing.

134
00:06:16.388 --> 00:06:17.327
Part 7.

135
00:06:17.607 --> 00:06:19.953
Phrases that help and phrases that hurt.

136
00:06:21.203 --> 00:06:22.569
Here is a quick table:

137
00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:24.470
Avoid, and Use instead.

138
00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:27.097
I need more money because my rent went up.:

139
00:06:27.377 --> 00:06:29.595
Based on my impact and market data...

140
00:06:29.875 --> 00:06:31.326
Whatever you think is fair.:

141
00:06:31.606 --> 00:06:34.166
I'm looking for around 58 lakh rupees.

142
00:06:34.446 --> 00:06:35.918
I'll leave if I don't get it.

143
00:06:36.198 --> 00:06:36.966
(threat):

144
00:06:37.246 --> 00:06:38.483
I want to grow here.

145
00:06:38.763 --> 00:06:40.257
What would make this possible?

146
00:06:40.537 --> 00:06:41.966
Sorry to ask, but...:

147
00:06:42.246 --> 00:06:43.526
I'd like to discuss...

148
00:06:43.806 --> 00:06:44.574
Okay.

149
00:06:44.854 --> 00:06:46.305
(accepting immediately):

150
00:06:46.585 --> 00:06:47.417
Thank you.

151
00:06:47.697 --> 00:06:50.150
Can I take a day to review the full package?

152
00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:52.094
A single exact low number:

153
00:06:52.374 --> 00:06:55.403
A researched range or a confident specific number.

154
00:06:56.753 --> 00:06:57.628
Part 8.

155
00:06:57.908 --> 00:06:58.975
Golden rules.

156
00:07:00.225 --> 00:07:01.142
Success:

157
00:07:01.422 --> 00:07:02.126
Do.

158
00:07:02.406 --> 00:07:07.099
Be enthusiastic about the role and firm on the number in the same conversation.

159
00:07:07.379 --> 00:07:08.446
Ask for time:

160
00:07:08.726 --> 00:07:11.307
Can I get back to you by Thursday? is normal.

161
00:07:11.587 --> 00:07:15.214
Get everything in writing before you resign from your current job.

162
00:07:15.494 --> 00:07:16.923
Negotiate once, well.

163
00:07:17.203 --> 00:07:18.995
Avoid going back again and again.

164
00:07:20.345 --> 00:07:21.263
Watch out:

165
00:07:21.543 --> 00:07:22.204
Don't.

166
00:07:22.484 --> 00:07:24.553
Lie about offers or current salary.

167
00:07:24.833 --> 00:07:29.121
Negotiate over chat or messages for the main discussion; prefer a call.

168
00:07:29.401 --> 00:07:32.879
Accept a counter-offer from your current employer purely for money.

169
00:07:33.159 --> 00:07:35.655
The reasons you wanted to leave usually remain.

170
00:07:35.935 --> 00:07:37.961
Burn bridges if it doesn't work out:

171
00:07:38.241 --> 00:07:39.500
Thank you for the offer.

172
00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:43.044
I'll have to decline this time, but I'd love to stay in touch.

173
00:07:44.394 --> 00:07:45.290
Part 9.

174
00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:47.469
Negotiation role-play prompt.

175
00:07:48.719 --> 00:07:50.596
Here is a template you can copy.

176
00:07:50.876 --> 00:07:52.903
Role-play a salary negotiation.

177
00:07:53.183 --> 00:07:55.785
You are an HR manager at a product company.

178
00:07:56.065 --> 00:07:56.919
Offer me.

179
00:07:57.199 --> 00:07:59.439
48 lakh per annum rupees for a.

180
00:07:59.719 --> 00:08:06.908
Senior Backend Engineer role (my target is 58 lakh per annum rupees, walk-away 50 lakh per annum rupees).

181
00:08:07.188 --> 00:08:12.436
Push back. realistically: budget is fixed, that's above our band, we need an answer today.

182
00:08:12.716 --> 00:08:13.761
After I type.

183
00:08:14.041 --> 00:08:18.201
DEBRIEF, score. my negotiation and rewrite my weakest reply.

184
00:08:21.051 --> 00:08:23.419
See the Master Prompt for the full coaching setup.

185
00:08:24.769 --> 00:08:25.623
Part 10.

186
00:08:25.903 --> 00:08:27.289
Practice conversation:

187
00:08:27.569 --> 00:08:28.764
Countering an offer.

188
00:08:30.014 --> 00:08:32.041
Here is how the conversation goes.

189
00:08:32.321 --> 00:08:35.179
We're happy to offer you 48 lakh rupees per year.

190
00:08:35.459 --> 00:08:38.873
Thank you, I'm really excited about this role and the team.

191
00:08:39.153 --> 00:08:40.070
Great!

192
00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:42.526
Can we expect your acceptance this week?

193
00:08:42.806 --> 00:08:45.409
I'd like to discuss the base salary first.

194
00:08:45.689 --> 00:08:52.366
Based on my experience and the market for this level, I was expecting closer to 58 lakh rupees.

195
00:08:52.646 --> 00:08:54.502
That's above our band for this role.

196
00:08:55.852 --> 00:08:57.452
The conversation continues.

197
00:08:57.732 --> 00:08:59.097
I understand.

198
00:08:59.377 --> 00:09:04.092
Is there any flexibility, perhaps with a joining bonus or extra ESOPs?

199
00:09:04.372 --> 00:09:09.087
I could check on a joining bonus of 4 lakh rupees and a review after six months.

200
00:09:09.367 --> 00:09:10.455
That would help.

201
00:09:10.735 --> 00:09:14.617
Could you also check if the base can go to 52 lakh rupees?

202
00:09:14.897 --> 00:09:17.265
If so, I'm ready to accept this week.

203
00:09:17.545 --> 00:09:19.679
Let me check and get back to you tomorrow.

204
00:09:21.029 --> 00:09:22.565
That's the end of this lesson.

205
00:09:22.845 --> 00:09:27.517
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

206
00:09:27.797 --> 00:09:33.898
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

